+# Nuvra AI Architecture — Phase 2.5: Intelligent Mock Generation
+
+**Author:** Manus AI
+**Date:** Feb 26, 2026
+
+---
+
+## 1. Overview
+
+This document details the architectural enhancements for Phase 2.5, which focused on making Nuvra’s mock AI provider feel genuinely intelligent. The goal was to improve prompt understanding, add a deliberate planning step, and support multi-page site generation — all without integrating real AI APIs.
+
+The core change is the introduction of a two-step “thinking” pipeline that happens *before* the `MockProvider` generates a schema.
+
+## 2. The Enhanced Mock Generation Pipeline
+
+The mock generation process now follows a more sophisticated, multi-stage pipeline:
+
+| Step | Component | Input | Output | Description |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| 1 | **Prompt Analyser** | `(prompt)` | `PromptIntent` | Extracts rich, structured intent from the raw user prompt, including page type, brand, industry, tone, and desired features. |
+| 2 | **Site Planner** | `PromptIntent` | `SitePlan` | Converts the `PromptIntent` into a structured plan, defining which pages to build and which sections each page should contain. |
+| 3 | **Mock Provider** | `SitePlan` | `PageSchema` | The provider now acts as a “content filler,” populating the section blueprints from the `SitePlan` with relevant, contextual content from its library. |
+| 4 | **Schema Renderer** | `PageSchema` | `{ html, css }` | (Unchanged) Renders the final HTML and CSS from the `PageSchema`. |
+
+This architecture separates prompt understanding from planning, and planning from content generation, making the mock AI’s behavior more transparent, predictable, and intelligent.
+
+```mermaid
+graph TD
+    A[User Prompt] --> B{1. PromptAnalyser};
+    B -- "Extracts" --> C(PromptIntent JSON);
+    C --> D{2. SitePlanner};
+    D -- "Decides" --> E(SitePlan JSON);
+    E --> F{3. MockProvider};
+    F -- "Fills" --> G(PageSchema JSON);
+    G --> H{4. SchemaRenderer};
+    H -- "Renders" --> I({html, css});
+    I --> J[GrapesJS Editor];
+```
+
+## 3. Core Components
+
+### 3.1. `PromptAnalyser` (`src/ai/promptAnalyser.js`)
+
+This new module replaces the simple keyword classifier from Phase 2. It performs a multi-dimensional analysis of the user’s prompt to produce a rich `PromptIntent` object.
+
+-   **Signal-Based Scoring**: It uses weighted keyword matching across multiple categories (page type, industry, tone) to determine the user’s primary intent.
+-   **Multi-Page Detection**: It looks for explicit signals (e.g., “full site,” “with home, about, and contact pages”) to determine if a multi-page site should be generated.
+-   **Brand Extraction**: It uses regex patterns to find brand names (e.g., “a website for Acme Corp,” “a landing page called FlowState”).
+-   **Transparent Output**: The resulting `PromptIntent` includes a `signals` array, which is a human-readable log of what the analyser detected and why, making debugging easy.
+
+### 3.2. `SitePlanner` (`src/ai/sitePlanner.js`)
+
+This module acts as the “brain” of the mock AI. It takes the `PromptIntent` and decides what to build.
+
+-   **Blueprint-Driven**: It uses a library of `SECTION_BLUEPRINTS` that define the ideal section order for different page types (e.g., a SaaS landing page should have a hero, then features, then a testimonial, then a CTA).
+-   **Multi-Page Structures**: It contains `MULTI_PAGE_STRUCTURES` that define which pages to generate for a given site type (e.g., a “SaaS” site gets Home, Pricing, About, and Contact pages).
+-   **Optional Section Injection**: It intelligently injects optional sections (like a pricing grid or FAQ) into the plan if the `PromptAnalyser` detected those features in the prompt.
+-   **Output**: The final output is a `SitePlan`, a clean, declarative object describing the entire site structure before any content is generated.
+
+### 3.3. `MockProvider` (`src/ai/mockProvider.js`)
+
+The `MockProvider` has been completely rewritten. It is no longer a collection of static templates. Instead, it is a **dynamic content assembler**.
+
+-   **Consumes the `SitePlan`**: Its primary job is to take the `SitePlan` and execute it.
+-   **Contextual Content Library**: It contains a rich library of content snippets (headlines, subtitles, feature items, testimonials) keyed by industry and section type.
+-   **Content Filling**: For each section in the `SitePlan`, it selects the appropriate content from its library based on the `PromptIntent`’s industry and tone, and uses it to fill the section’s properties.
+-   **Multi-Page Support**: It now has two primary methods: `mockGenerate` (for single pages) and `mockGenerateSite` (for multi-page sites).
+
+## 4. API and UI Changes
+
+-   **`aiEngine.js`**: A new public function, `generateSite(prompt, options)`, has been added. It orchestrates the multi-page generation flow and returns an array of `SiteGenerationResult` objects.
+-   **`app.js`**: A new event handler has been added for the “Generate Site” button. It calls `generateSite()` and then iterates through the results, adding each generated page to the `pageManager`.
+-   **`index.html`**: A “Generate Site” button has been added to the top bar, and the prompt placeholder text has been updated to encourage both single-page and multi-page generation.
+
+## 5. Design Benefits
+
+| Decision | Rationale | Benefit |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **Analyser → Planner → Builder** | Separating prompt understanding, planning, and content generation makes the system more modular and easier to reason about. | **Intelligence & Transparency.** The mock AI’s decisions are no longer a black box. The console logs from the analyser and planner show exactly why a certain structure was chosen. |
+| **Blueprint-Based Planning** | Defining ideal section orders in blueprints enforces proven UX patterns and ensures high-quality page structures. | **Structural Quality.** Generated pages have a logical flow that is optimized for their purpose (e.g., conversion, information, portfolio). |
+| **Contextual Content Library** | Keying content snippets by industry allows the mock provider to generate highly relevant and realistic text. | **Content Relevance.** A prompt for a “fintech startup” will now generate content about security and compliance, while a prompt for a “design portfolio” will generate content about creativity and process. |
+| **Dedicated Multi-Page Flow** | Creating a separate `generateSite` function and a `SitePlan` object makes multi-page generation a first-class citizen. | **Scalability.** The architecture now naturally supports generating entire websites, not just individual pages, which is a critical step towards building a true site builder. |
+
+This phase successfully makes the mock AI feel surprisingly intelligent, providing a high-quality user experience even before connecting to a real LLM. The architecture is now robust enough to serve as a solid foundation for all future AI-facing AI features.
