++/**
++ * Nuvra Builder — Publish Manager  (Phase 5)
++ *
++ * Orchestrates the full publish flow:
++ *   1. Show the Publish modal with a build summary
++ *   2. Let the user name their site and confirm
++ *   3. Run the SiteBuilder to produce the file bundle
++ *   4. Package the bundle into a ZIP using fflate (loaded from CDN)
++ *   5. Trigger a browser download of the ZIP
++ *   6. Show a build report (success / warnings)
++ *
++ * ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
++ * │  Publish Flow                                                            │
++ * │                                                                          │
++ * │  User clicks "Publish"                                                   │
++ * │    → PublishModal opens (shows page list, site name input)              │
++ * │    → User clicks "Build & Download"                                     │
++ * │    → Progress bar updates as each page is rendered                      │
++ * │    → ZIP is assembled in memory                                         │
++ * │    → Browser downloads <site-name>.zip                                  │
++ * │    → Build report modal shows success / warnings                        │
++ * └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
++ *
++ * Design decisions:
++ *  - ZIP generation uses `fflate` (loaded from CDN via a dynamic import).
++ *    fflate is a pure-JS, zero-dependency ZIP library that works entirely
++ *    in the browser with no build step. It is the lightest option available.
++ *  - The ZIP is assembled entirely in memory and never touches the filesystem.
++ *    This keeps the publish flow instant and avoids any server dependency.
++ *  - The PublishManager is stateless. Each call to `openPublishModal()` is
++ *    a fresh, independent publish session.
++ *  - Error handling is granular: individual page failures produce warnings
++ *    but do not abort the build. The user receives a full report.
++ */
++
